3.3 Installing IBM Software Hub OADP backup and restore

If IBM Software Hub is deployed on a Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform cluster, install backup and restore components by doing the following steps.

    Log in to Red Hat OpenShift Container Platform as a cluster administrator.

    ${OC_LOGIN}

    Remember: OC_LOGIN is an alias for the oc login command.
    Use the following command to create the ${OADP_PROJECT} project where you want to install the OADP operator.

    oc new-project ${OADP_PROJECT}

    Annotate the ${OADP_PROJECT} project so that Kopia pods can be scheduled on all nodes.

    oc annotate namespace ${OADP_PROJECT} openshift.io/node-selector=""

    Install the Red Hat OADP operator and DataProtectionApplication (DPA) custom resource.

    You can install the OADP operator and DPA either automatically using the cpd-cli oadp install command or manually.

    You must use the manual method in the following scenarios:
        You already have the OADP operator installed
        You use an object store that is not S3-compatible or it does not use an S3 style path
        You use a Red Hat OpenShift Service on AWS (ROSA) cluster with Security Token Service (STS).

